      "pdfPages": [
        76
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 12,
      "questionId": "qe-c07-0094",
      "sentenceId": "c07-s05-p076-01725-s002",
      "sentenceText": "The philosopher Jason D’Cruz has written about planned vs. unplanned actions using the term “volatile reason.”",
      "sentenceSha256": "9c3c6e24abfb8ff4f89d06a07c15f6d8b167ac32ceedc1435863ab0c4b4a143d",
      "readingUnitId": "c07-s05-p076-01725-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c07-057",
      "parentFingerprint": "371f466f21356f9331de1905ea11fdf0fdc026033fd034a31d2e536bc6906393",
      "passageSha256": "d70f597e949be92351f89d00f9e4de7a0e8d91db84d393bf6ae8f2b82b456f5e",
      "pdfPages": [
        76
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 13,
      "questionId": "qe-c07-0095",
      "sentenceId": "c07-s05-p076-01725-s004",
      "sentenceText": "In this scenario, Moritz has a ticket for a train ride from Berlin to Dresden to meet his friends.",
      "sentenceSha256": "aed0ead27d77c367f31735e9c6965b8613fe4f4c8b8888cfeb688aab442c1369",
      "readingUnitId": "c07-s05-p076-01725-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c07-057",
      "parentFingerprint": "371f466f21356f9331de1905ea11fdf0fdc026033fd034a31d2e536bc6906393",
      "passageSha256": "d70f597e949be92351f89d00f9e4de7a0e8d91db84d393bf6ae8f2b82b456f5e",
      "pdfPages": [
        76
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 14,
      "questionId": "qe-c07-0096",
      "sentenceId": "c07-s05-p076-01725-s005",
      "sentenceText": "His friends are preparing a dinner, and Moritz has tickets to a concert for him and his friends that evening; in other words, he has a plan and responsibilities.",
      "sentenceSha256": "0cd87b1ef29d5662acf1b941402afb90994ee02b0c3eb93baef57b39503ca8cb",
      "readingUnitId": "c07-s05-p076-01725-r005-007",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c07-058",
      "parentFingerprint": "550f417956f5f3bdbd00711c3b42866c8a752fbecf65cfc48af9d7b6fdd63b02",
      "passageSha256": "a0cabefcb2885340cb4a1a11471ae9ba3c458107dadc571755421e9eecd90b59",
      "pdfPages": [
        76
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 15,
      "questionId": "qe-c07-0097",
      "sentenceId": "c07-s05-p076-01725-s006",
      "sentenceText": "On the train, however, he sees the train schedule and realizes that he could go on to the unknown city of Zittau if he stays on past Dresden.",
      "sentenceSha256": "540c8246788f6c6f0d268036745abd2c56a92671457e5a2b9b63a039027db9bd",
      "readingUnitId": "c07-s05-p076-01725-r005-007",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c07-058",
      "parentFingerprint": "550f417956f5f3bdbd00711c3b42866c8a752fbecf65cfc48af9d7b6fdd63b02",
      "passageSha256": "a0cabefcb2885340cb4a1a11471ae9ba3c458107dadc571755421e9eecd90b59",
      "pdfPages": [
        76
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 16,
      "questionId": "qe-c07-0098",
      "sentenceId": "c07-s05-p076-01725-s008",
      "sentenceText": "Right after the train leaves Dresden, Moritz feels an overwhelming euphoria and a powerful sensation of freedom.",
      "sentenceSha256": "4f2d237aae3318a9dd158da011fc9f1a49778725b6af9929e05b54fd5b14c3b5",
      "readingUnitId": "c07-s05-p076-01725-r008-011",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c07-059",
      "parentFingerprint": "ca9aa98b87759ceaa7ac8783581d303d115689ca9a3c9581f6b616b736c60d7e",
      "passageSha256": "22e3b616e3d3ce8f40708f2fcf477f583887caa831b9df3fd1794713e53933e2",
      "pdfPages": [
        76
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 17,
      "questionId": "qe-c07-0099",
      "sentenceId": "c07-s05-p076-01725-s010",
      "sentenceText": "Spontaneity over responsibility.",
      "sentenceSha256": "f438a95781d5f6b428a0922f77c01ce2b1d2790b945dbef34fd668d1a1e2495f",
      "readingUnitId": "c07-s05-p076-01725-r008-011",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c07-059",
